# Symbolic k2 analysis (PR 12): the kernel's FLOPs and global bytes per
# thread as expressions in K, all behind the bounds guard (hence `<=`).
# Hand-derivation: main loop 8 flops/16 B per iteration x
# (K - K mod 4)/4 trips, remainder 2/4 x (K mod 4), epilogue 3 flops +
# 2 B load + 2 B store.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k2/k2.sm_80.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z15hgemm_coalescediiifPK6__halfS1_fPS_( // per thread: flops f32 <= (2·(param_2 mod 4) + 8·((param_2 - param_2 mod 4) / 4) + 3); global load <= (4·(param_2 mod 4) + 16·((param_2 - param_2 mod 4) / 4) + 2) B, store <= 2 B; param load 44 B{{$}}
